{
  "analysis": "I now understand the ELF loader: vm.js reads doomgeneric_mips, loads only .text, .data, and .rodata sections into memory as little-endian 32-bit words, finds the `main` symbol, and starts execution there. This means the ELF must be 32-bit little-endian MIPS with section headers and a main symbol. The compiler is /usr/bin/mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc-12. I need to inspect the syscall convention and run loop before building, because the VM is a simplified emulator and may not support glibc startup or all MIPS instructions.",
  "plan": "Inspect the syscall handler and instruction dispatch/run loop in vm.js to confirm syscall numbers, argument registers, and supported instructions. Then list the source files needed for a doomgeneric_img build and attempt a static MIPS build.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"runProgram\\|executeInstruction\\|handleSyscall\\|syscallNum\\|registers\\[2\\]\\|registers\\[4\\]\\|registers\\[7\\]\" /app/vm.js | head -220\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk 'NR>=1000 && NR<=1120 {print NR \":\" $0}' /app/vm.js\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk 'NR>=1120 && NR<=1265 {print NR \":\" $0}' /app/vm.js\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk 'NR>=1265 && NR<=1695 {print NR \":\" $0}' /app/vm.js | head -220\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric && ls *.c | grep -v -E 'doomgeneric_(xlib|sdl|win|allegro|emscripten|soso|sosox)\\.c|i_(sdlmusic|sdlsound|allegromusic|allegrosound)\\.c' | tr '\\n' ' '; echo\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
